---
title: Backup and restore
---
sequenceDiagram
  %% Source for 18-backup-restore-flow.html. Edit this file, then run ./scripts/render-diagrams.py.
  %% Directives: docs in diagrams/README.md (Updating diagrams).
  %% @subtitle Validated, checksummed backups and a restore that never drops the existing database first
  %% @type database: PG BK
  actor OP as Operator
  participant BS as backup-databases.py
  participant PG as PostgreSQL<br/>litellm_prod · litellm_dev · vector_store
  participant BK as backups/
  participant RS as restore-databases.py

  OP->>BS: run a backup
  par each database
    BS->>PG: dump litellm_prod
  and
    BS->>PG: dump litellm_dev
  and
    BS->>PG: dump vector_store
  end
  PG-->>BS: archives
  BS->>BS: validate with pg_restore and write SHA256SUMS
  BS->>BK: atomically publish
  OP->>RS: restore --confirm-restore
  RS->>BK: read a verified archive
  RS->>PG: restore into a staging database
  alt tables not restored
    RS--xOP: target left untouched
  else tables restored
    RS->>PG: rename target to *_pre_restore_*, promote staging
    RS-->>OP: restored, rerun the stack checks
  end
